```modelica
connector Pin
  Real v;
  flow Real i;
end Pin;
model Branch
  Pin p;
  Pin n;
end Branch;
model Study
  Pin boundary;
  Branch L;
  Branch G;
  Branch C2;
  Branch Nr;
equation
  connect(boundary, L.p);
  connect(L.p, G.p);
  connect(G.p, C2.p);
  connect(G.n, Nr.p);
end Study;
```

Question:
Within the equation scope of model instance Study, return the canonical signed member vector for the primitive flow connection set formed by explicit connect statements in that scope that contains boundary.i.

Target:
boundary.i

Answer format:
Use ascending path:integer entries joined by commas without spaces; coefficients must be primitive, nonzero, and oriented so the first coefficient is positive.
